\label{def:filtration}
(Filtration of a cosheaf) A filtration of $\mathcal{F}$ is a sequence of cosheaves $\left\{ \mathcal{F}_{i}\right\} ^{n}_{i=0}$ where $\mathcal{F}_{n}=\mathcal{F}$ equipped with an injective morphism between any two consecutive indices, meaning for every $0\leq i\leq n-1$, there exists a morphism $\psi^{i}:\mathcal{F}_{i}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{F}_{i+1}$, such that we get - 
\[
\mathcal{F}_{0}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{F}_{1}\dots\hookrightarrow\mathcal{F}_{n-1}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{F}_{n}=\mathcal{F}
\]

\label{def:homology_group}
For every filtration level $0\leq i\leq n$ and for every dimension $k$, we define the $k$-th homology group of the complex as the quotient of the cycle space by the boundary space: 
$H_{k}(K;\mathcal{F}_{i})=\frac{\ker\left(\partial^{\mathcal{F}_{i}}_{k}\right)}{\operatorname{Im}\left(\partial^{\mathcal{F}_{i}}_{k+1}\right)}$
